# Port vs matching source

`src/` is the source of truth for game behavior (byte-matching Borland build).
`port/` is a separate SDL3 rewrite. Do not change matching shape in `src/` to
suit the port.

## When changing port code

1. Find the corresponding logic in `src/` (same module name when possible:
   `port/src/between.c` ↔ `src/between.c`).
2. Prefer a close transcription of that logic over re-deriving behavior.
3. Mark clear correspondences with a one-line comment:
   `/* orig: Name (SSSS:OOOO) */`
   using the address from the matching `// FUNCTION:` line. One comment can
   cover a cluster of helpers that implement one original function.
4. Do not put matching `// FUNCTION: AARCADE …` annotations in `port/`; those
   are for `necmp.py` / the Borland tree only.
5. Port-only helpers (SDL layout, textures) need no orig line.
